Event Handling:
Event handling in react is used to handle the user interactions such submit a 
form,enter a userinput, clicking a button 
the common event handlers are onClick, onSubmit, onChange 

onChange: when user enter input such as username, password
          the onChange event will capture the user input 

onSubmit: onsubmit is used to handle the submit a form data such as save,
           for example when submitting a login or registration form.  

onClick: onClick is used to handle the click an element as button. 
         for example if i have a view detail button to see the vendor details 
         user clicks on view button it will fetch the user details .

onChange → User changes data ✍️
onClick → User clicks something 🖱️
onSubmit → User submits a form 📤



func app(){
    const [username, setUserName] = useState("")
    const [password, setPassword] = useState("")

    const {handleSubmit} => ()
    {
        event.preventDefault();

    console.log(username);
    console.log(password);
    }
    return(
        <form submit={handleSubmit}>
        <input type = "text"
               value = {username}
               onChange{(e) => setUserName(e.target.value)}
               placeholder = "password"
        />
        <input type = "text"
               value = {password}
               onChange{(e) => setPassword(e.target.value)}
               placeholder = "password"
        />
        <button type = "button"> submit </button>
        </form>
    )

}